WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.090
Groundwater is a map problem before it is a
numbers problem —

2
00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:07.498
what your neighbour's well is doing matters to
yours.

3
00:00:07.618 --> 00:00:11.338
MyWell has two maps, and they work the same
way.

4
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:14.958
Now we're on: My station map.

5
00:00:15.078 --> 00:00:18.078
A map of just the stations you look after.

6
00:00:18.198 --> 00:00:24.390
Tap any pin to see its latest reading, and use the
filters along the top to focus on one type,

7
00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:26.310
or one station.

8
00:00:27.117 --> 00:00:29.133
Your monitoring areas.

9
00:00:29.253 --> 00:00:32.469
A monitoring area is a saved set of stations.

10
00:00:32.589 --> 00:00:38.109
Open My Monitoring Areas to switch between
“All stations” and any area you've saved,

11
00:00:38.229 --> 00:00:40.605
or the built-in Example area.

12
00:00:41.417 --> 00:00:43.193
Filter by type.

13
00:00:43.313 --> 00:00:50.417
Open Station type to show or hide each kind of
station — groundwater wells, rainfall, check-dams,

14
00:00:50.537 --> 00:00:52.313
rivers and more.

15
00:00:52.433 --> 00:00:54.785
It doubles as the map legend.

16
00:00:55.617 --> 00:00:57.897
Find specific stations.

17
00:00:58.017 --> 00:01:04.113
Use Station to search by name or code and pick just
the stations you want; the map narrows to them.

18
00:01:04.917 --> 00:01:06.693
Build an area.

19
00:01:06.813 --> 00:01:12.861
Actions is how you create an area: Pick
stations one by one, Draw an area on the map,

20
00:01:12.981 --> 00:01:15.861
or Select area by dragging a box.

21
00:01:15.981 --> 00:01:19.269
Save it and it appears in My Monitoring Areas.

22
00:01:20.083 --> 00:01:23.011
Now we're on: Stations on map.

23
00:01:23.131 --> 00:01:25.795
Every shared station in one place.

24
00:01:25.915 --> 00:01:32.611
Filter, search, group stations into Monitoring Areas, and
read a chart of whatever the map is showing.

25
00:01:33.417 --> 00:01:35.433
Your monitoring areas.

26
00:01:35.553 --> 00:01:38.769
A monitoring area is a saved set of stations.

27
00:01:38.889 --> 00:01:44.409
Open My Monitoring Areas to switch between
“All stations” and any area you've saved,

28
00:01:44.529 --> 00:01:46.905
or the built-in Example area.

29
00:01:47.717 --> 00:01:49.493
Filter by type.

30
00:01:49.613 --> 00:01:56.717
Open Station type to show or hide each kind of
station — groundwater wells, rainfall, check-dams,

31
00:01:56.837 --> 00:01:58.613
rivers and more.

32
00:01:58.733 --> 00:02:01.085
It doubles as the map legend.

33
00:02:01.917 --> 00:02:04.197
Find specific stations.

34
00:02:04.317 --> 00:02:10.413
Use Station to search by name or code and pick just
the stations you want; the map narrows to them.

35
00:02:11.217 --> 00:02:12.993
Build an area.

36
00:02:13.113 --> 00:02:19.161
Actions is how you create an area: Pick
stations one by one, Draw an area on the map,

37
00:02:19.281 --> 00:02:22.161
or Select area by dragging a box.

38
00:02:22.281 --> 00:02:25.569
Save it and it appears in My Monitoring Areas.

39
00:02:26.383 --> 00:02:28.327
That is the whole page.

40
00:02:28.447 --> 00:02:33.103
You can replay this tutorial any time from the
Learning page inside the app.

41
00:02:33.223 --> 00:02:36.199
Thanks for helping look after our groundwater.
